    "summary": "I built a single-cell planter. A vertical riser comes up through the floor of the base at (0,0,0). It feeds a full-depth drained bin with a PVC bore, which is the bin made for a pipe passing through it. I filled the bin with soil and put in one plug plant. To follow the house rules I added solid end caps on all six side faces. There were no joints to bolt because there is only one cell. The build is 8 parts, about 559 g of filament and roughly 779 minutes of printing. The configurator's checks passed with no rule issues, and its collision check came back clear. It only checks fit. It can't tell whether the parts will hold water without leaking.",
